{{ 'learning-hub.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}

<section class="learning-hub learning-preview-shell color-{{ section.settings.color_scheme }} gradient">
  <div class="learning-preview-note page-width" role="note">
    <p class="learning-hub__eyebrow">Development Preview</p>
    <p>This fixture-backed preview is for Stage 6 visual QA only and must be removed before production launch.</p>
  </div>

  <div id="LearningHubPreviewRoot" aria-live="polite">
    <div class="page-width learning-panel">
      <p class="learning-empty">Loading Learning Hub preview fixtures.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{% comment %}
  The fixture data <script src> tag is generated into a tiny pointer snippet
  (learning-hub-preview-data-script-tag.liquid) that names a content-hashed
  asset filename (learning-hub-preview-data.<hash>.js), and that pointer
  snippet is rendered inline here on this always-dynamic page (confirmed
  cf-cache-status: DYNAMIC, never cached) rather than hardcoded. Confirmed via
  direct Admin API comparison against served CDN bytes that Shopify's
  theme-asset CDN caches by path only, ignoring the `?v=` query string
  entirely (a never-before-seen query string still came back as a cache HIT),
  with an observed ~1 year max-age -- a content-only re-push of a FIXED
  filename can leave the edge serving a stale response indefinitely with no
  query-string workaround. Content-hashing the filename means the CDN has
  genuinely never cached that exact path before whenever content changes.
  Regenerate both files with `npm run learning:generate-preview-fixture`
  (from shopify/) -- never hand-edit either one.
{% endcomment %}
{% render 'learning-hub-preview-data-script-tag' %}
<script src="{{ 'learning-hub-preview.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>
{% comment %}
  learning-hub-preview.js itself is still a cached static asset (hand-authored,
  not regenerated) and would hit the same staleness risk described above if
  its contents are ever edited -- re-pushing alone will not be enough to make
  a change visible. If that happens, apply the same inline-snippet treatment
  used above, or ask for a fresh Admin API byte comparison before assuming a
  push took effect.
{% endcomment %}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Learning Hub dev preview",
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "color_scheme",
      "id": "color_scheme",
      "label": "Color scheme",
      "default": "scheme-1"
    }
  ],
  "presets": [
    {
      "name": "Learning Hub dev preview"
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
